.TH FL-FLATPAK 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-flatpak \- Flatpak apps for fldesktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-flatpak\fR [\fIAPP-ID\fR [\fB\-\-tab\fR \fBfiles\fR|\fBdepends\fR|\fBused-by\fR]]
.br
\fBfl-flatpak\fR \fIFILE\fR.flatpakref | \fIFILE\fR.flatpakrepo | \fIFILE\fR.flatpak
.br
\fBfl-flatpak \-\-prefs\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the apps of the configured Flatpak sources (Flathub and others) with
their icons, descriptions, licenses and versions, by category, installed or
with an update, and searches them. Apps can be installed for all users or
only for you, opened, updated (one or all) and removed. When Flathub is not
set up, fl-flatpak offers to add it.
.PP
\fBPermissions…\fR shows what an installed app may use (network, display,
sound, devices, files and folders...) and changes it for you, like
\fBflatpak override \-\-user\fR: the changes are written to
\fI~/.local/share/flatpak/overrides/APP-ID\fR and apply when the app starts
next.
.PP
The \fBFiles\fR, \fBDepends on\fR and \fBUsed by\fR tabs of an installed app
or runtime list its files, the runtime (or, for an extension, the ref it
extends) it needs, and the installed apps and extensions that need it.
\fBRuntimes\fR lists the installed runtimes and extensions.
.PP
Given a .flatpakref, .flatpak bundle or .flatpakrepo file, fl-flatpak
installs the app or adds the source.
.PP
Installing for all users asks for an administrator password through
\fBfl-polkit-agent\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBflatpak\fR(1), \fBflatpak-override\fR(1), \fBfl-packages\fR(1)
.SH SOURCES AND SETTINGS
\fBSources and Settings\fR (or \fB\-\-prefs\fR) lists the sources (remotes) of
the system and the user installation. Sources can be added by address or from
a \fI.flatpakrepo\fR, edited (title, priority), enabled, disabled and removed;
changes to the system installation ask for an administrator (polkit). The
General tab sets where apps are installed by default and whether the catalogs
are downloaded at every start, and removes unused runtimes or repairs an
installation (\fBflatpak repair\fR). The settings are kept in
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/flatpak.ini\fR.
